        "question_count": 2,
        "questions": [
          {
            "question_index": 1,
            "question_type": "multiple-choice",
            "answer_cardinality": "single",
            "prompt_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "What is $c_1$ for $x(t)=6\\cos(\\omega_0 t+\\pi/6)$?",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              }
            ],
            "choices": [
              {
                "choice_label": "A",
                "choice_blocks": [
                  {
                    "block_type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "$3e^{j\\pi/6}$",
                    "latex": "",
                    "image_slot_id": ""
                  }
                ],
                "is_correct": true
              },
              {
                "choice_label": "B",
                "choice_blocks": [
                  {
                    "block_type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "$6e^{j\\pi/6}$",
                    "latex": "",
                    "image_slot_id": ""
                  }
                ],
                "is_correct": false
              },
              {
                "choice_label": "C",
                "choice_blocks": [
                  {
                    "block_type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "$3e^{-j\\pi/6}$",
                    "latex": "",
                    "image_slot_id": ""
                  }
                ],
                "is_correct": false
              },
              {
                "choice_label": "D",
                "choice_blocks": [
                  {
                    "block_type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "$6e^{-j\\pi/6}$",
                    "latex": "",
                    "image_slot_id": ""
                  }
                ],
                "is_correct": false
              },
              {
                "choice_label": "E",
                "choice_blocks": [
                  {
                    "block_type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "$3$",
                    "latex": "",
                    "image_slot_id": ""
                  }
                ],
                "is_correct": false
              }
            ],
            "correct_choice_labels": [
              "A"
            ],
            "correct_answer": "$3e^{j\\pi/6}$",
            "answer_explanation_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "Expand the cosine as half the sum of complex exponentials, so the amplitude becomes $3$ instead of $6$. After multiplying by $e^{-j\\omega_0 t}$, the matching $k=1$ term stays constant and the nonmatching term averages to zero over one period.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              },
              {
                "block_type": "display-math",
                "text": "",
                "latex": "\\begin{aligned}\n6\\cos(\\omega_0 t+\\pi/6) &= 3\\left(e^{j(\\omega_0 t+\\pi/6)}+e^{-j(\\omega_0 t+\\pi/6)}\\right) \\\\\nc_1 &= \\frac{1}{T}\\int_0^T 6\\cos(\\omega_0 t+\\pi/6)e^{-j\\omega_0 t}\\,dt \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{T}\\int_0^T 3\\left(e^{j(\\omega_0 t+\\pi/6)}+e^{-j(\\omega_0 t+\\pi/6)}\\right)e^{-j\\omega_0 t}\\,dt \\\\\n&= 3e^{j\\pi/6}\n\\end{aligned}",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              },
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "So $c_1=3e^{j\\pi/6}$. The choice with the full amplitude misses the $1/2$ from the cosine expansion, the opposite-phase choice is the $k=-1$ coefficient, and the pure number ignores the phase weight.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "question_index": 2,
            "question_type": "multiple-choice",
            "answer_cardinality": "single",
            "prompt_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "What is $c_1$ for $x(t)=-8\\cos(\\omega_0 t-\\pi/4)$?",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              }
            ],
            "choices": [
              {
                "choice_label": "A",
                "choice_blocks": [
                  {
                    "block_type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "$-4e^{-j\\pi/4}$",
                    "latex": "",
                    "image_slot_id": ""
                  }
                ],
                "is_correct": true
              },
              {
                "choice_label": "B",
                "choice_blocks": [
                  {
                    "block_type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "$-8e^{-j\\pi/4}$",
                    "latex": "",
                    "image_slot_id": ""
                  }
                ],
                "is_correct": false
              },
              {
                "choice_label": "C",
                "choice_blocks": [
                  {
                    "block_type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "$-4e^{j\\pi/4}$",
                    "latex": "",
                    "image_slot_id": ""
                  }
                ],
                "is_correct": false
              },
              {
                "choice_label": "D",
                "choice_blocks": [
                  {
                    "block_type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "$-8e^{j\\pi/4}$",
                    "latex": "",
                    "image_slot_id": ""
                  }
                ],
                "is_correct": false
              },
              {
                "choice_label": "E",
                "choice_blocks": [
                  {
                    "block_type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "$4e^{-j\\pi/4}$",
                    "latex": "",
                    "image_slot_id": ""
                  }
                ],
                "is_correct": false
              }
            ],
            "correct_choice_labels": [
              "A"
            ],
            "correct_answer": "$-4e^{-j\\pi/4}$",
            "answer_explanation_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "The negative amplitude stays outside the cosine, and the cosine still contributes a half-amplitude coefficient. After you expand and multiply by $e^{-j\\omega_0 t}$, only the matching harmonic remains.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              },
              {
                "block_type": "display-math",
                "text": "",
                "latex": "\\begin{aligned}\n-8\\cos(\\omega_0 t-\\pi/4) &= -4\\left(e^{j(\\omega_0 t-\\pi/4)}+e^{-j(\\omega_0 t-\\pi/4)}\\right) \\\\\nc_1 &= \\frac{1}{T}\\int_0^T -8\\cos(\\omega_0 t-\\pi/4)e^{-j\\omega_0 t}\\,dt \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{T}\\int_0^T -4\\left(e^{j(\\omega_0 t-\\pi/4)}+e^{-j(\\omega_0 t-\\pi/4)}\\right)e^{-j\\omega_0 t}\\,dt \\\\\n&= -4e^{-j\\pi/4}\n\\end{aligned}",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              },
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "So $c_1=-4e^{-j\\pi/4}$. The choice with the full amplitude misses the $1/2$, the opposite-phase choice is the conjugate harmonic, the full-amplitude opposite-phase choice combines both mistakes, and the positive answer drops the sign on the original cosine.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "lesson_index": 6,
        "lesson_title": "Complex-Valued Fourier Coefficients",
