            "correct_answer": "They are conjugate partners that together encode one real $k=4$ harmonic; the positive coefficient carries the amplitude-and-phase weight.",
            "answer_explanation_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "Because the signal is real, $c_4$ and $c_{-4}$ must be conjugates. They do not represent two different harmonics; together they form one real oscillation, and the positive-index coefficient is the one whose magnitude and phase tell you the harmonic weight.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              }
